==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|p|ä}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*pää}}, from {{inh|fi|urj-pro|*päŋe}}. Cognates include Estonian {{m|et|pea}}, Veps {{m|vep|pä}} and Hungarian {{m|hu|fej}}, {{m|hu|fő}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|lang=fi|/pæː/}}
* {{rhymes|æː|lang=fi}}
* {{hyphenation|pää|lang=fi}}

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# [[head]] (of an organism or organisation)
# [[end]], [[tip]] (physical end)

====Declension====
Note:  The noun ''pää'' with its usual meaning is '''defective''' and missing the outer local cases, for which the inner local cases are '''always''' substituted in correct usage.

The outer local cases  '''päälle, päällä, päältä,''' in the singular only, are very common '''postpositions with an entirely different meaning.'''

{{fi-decl-maa|pää|ä}}

